The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
task_lock(p);
pol = p->mempolicy;
mpol_get(pol);
```
Reason:
These statements involve unnecessary locking of the task and management of the memory policy, which were required for the older format of `/proc/pid/sched`. Since the format has changed, these operations are no longer needed, leading to inefficiencies and increased complexity in the code.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
// Removed the task_lock(p);
// Removed the memory policy management (pol = p->mempolicy; mpol_get(pol);)
```
Reason:
By removing the task locking and memory policy management, the function `sched_show_numa()` is simplified, eliminating redundant operations that are no longer necessary due to the updated format of the `/proc/pid/sched` output. This leads to cleaner and more efficient code.

